      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T19:22:57Z",
      "note": "Reviewed both Ethereum setLatestData transactions, their receipts, full call traces and state diffs; the later drain receipt and trace; the Delegator creation; all five pre-incident upgrade calls; the exact contracts[9] storage transition; the selected NotarizationSerializer creation and historical runtime; CertiK's cross-chain reconstruction; and incident-time prices. Both notarization calls delegate from 0x71518580f36feceffe0721f06ba4703218cd7f63 through VerusNotarizer 0x9ce91aa0f6d1d316a9535a36951143bc141318b8 into NotarizationSerializer 0x95b8005c4d9fe80f0aee5b7adce53766080600fb selector 0x24f2cf86. The first call installs the poisoned candidate; the anchored second call confirms it and is therefore the failure-finalizing execution. The serializer loop overwrites stateRoot for every matching system ID, unlike Verus's first-entry map semantics. contracts[9], at keccak256(slot 13)+9, changed from 0x0a8c5a442b5f1aa7933e4db401ed1824a3423932 to the selected artifact in transaction 0xb29f45f3c788cc635fe746754dfe79b00f36758cbd9f418e69866e72c08e192d and remained unchanged through the anchor. The artifact was created at block 25501813 in transaction 0xbb17d79661c5458cab5aea108c71645530a1e3889d6787387e63348d33fefef4:3; its 11,750-byte runtime hashes to 0x7af074381469f2eeb4d02cfbd6bfdf966b26d6d3cc220a9c79b6c47515dfb711. The payout transaction moves exactly 1,137.45281584 ETH, 71.5045915 tBTC, 220,357.02707298 DAI, 59.42954384 MKR, 149,275.074098 USDC, 78,300.537681 USDT, 31,475.664323 EURC and 92,784.36027725 scrvUSD to the attacker's receiver."
